<html>
<title>Video Dump</title>
<body>

<h1>Video Dump</h1>
<p>
All emulators with video output can save the screen to a file. The Video Dump controls are shown below.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/video_dump.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Save</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>File name</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>VideoDump</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
To save the screen output to a file, press the <strong>Save</strong> button (1) or the <tt>F5</tt> key (only available while an emulator is running).
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> By default, the file name <tt>screendump.x.png</tt> (Portable Network Graphics image) will be used where <tt>x</tt> will count up from <tt>1</tt> for every new screen dump.
</p>

<p>
To change the output file name, type a new name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field (2). To change the directory location or file name, use the <strong>VideoDump</strong> button (3) and select another directory or file in the file selector window.
</p>

<p>
By default, the file will be stored in the emulator directory (located in the application data directory). See the <a href="MainFile.htm">Directory and File Structure</a> section.
</p>

<p>
To save in a different image format, change the file extension. The following extensions are supported: <tt>.png</tt> (Portable Network Graphics image), <tt>.jpeg</tt> (JPEG image), <tt>.bmp</tt> (Bitmap image), and <tt>.pcx</tt> (Paintbrush image).
</p>

</body>
</html>
